run.sh, run_nr.sh, run_r.sh and multirun*.sh find the executables in
build/bin of the CMake build of this tree, or in $ONCVPSP_BIN_DIR.  The
*_test.sh scripts and nist_test.py are run by ctest (tests/CMakeLists.txt);
run_test.sh runs an input once for the tests that read its output (the
fixtures run_<rel>_<input>).

compare_output.py compares two outputs quantity by quantity, parsed with
pyoncvpsp and upf-tools (ref_test.sh and the tests of outputs that must be
the same use it; doc/developer_setup.md, Tests). kernel_diff.py compares
pseudopotentials by their nonlocal kernels and local potentials, with the
standard library only; it and ref_patch.py are for changes of the reference
outputs.

smooth_scan.py steps one input through a fine window and measures how
smoothly the pseudopotential follows it (doc/smoothness_plan.md); ctest runs
it with the label smooth.

reindent.py re-indents the Fortran sources in the layout of
doc/coding_standards.md; pre-commit runs it, and with --stdin an editor
can run it as a formatter (doc/developer_setup.md).
